    <VI_Package_Configuration_File>Abstract Data Classes.vipc</VI_Package_Configuration_File>
    <Description>
      <One_Line_Description_Summary>A set of abstract classes for each of LabVIEWs strict types</One_Line_Description_Summary>
      <Description> LV_Abstract is a set of Abstract classes for almost all LabVIEW data types, and now 1D array types, including:
Boolean
Boolean 1D
String
String 1D
Single
Single 1D
Double
Double 1D
Extended
Extended 1D
Complex Single
Complex Single 1D
Complex Double
Complex Double 1D
Complex Extended
Complex Extended 1D
I8
I8 1D
I16
I16 1D
I32
I32 1D
I64
I64 1D
U8
U8 1D
U16
U16 1D
U32
U32 1D
U64
U64 1D
Time Stamp
Time Stamp 1D
Variant
Variant 1D
Waveform
Waveform 1D

Plus a set of Constants, Simple Variables. Each with a matching polymorphic VI to simplify usage.

Check out the 'API Tree.vi' for a complete outline off all classes, methods and properties</Description>
      <Copyright/>
      <Packager>Tim Streeter</Packager>
      <URL>https://github.com/timstreeter/LV_Abstract</URL>
      <Release_Notes>Now supporting from LabVIEW 2019
Changed to a more permissive BSD 3-Clause licensing
More complete Palette set
Added:
- Array Type
- 1D Array Type
- Boolean 1D Type
- String 1D
- Variant 1D
- Waveform 1D
- Numeric 1D
- Float 1D
- Integer 1D
- Double Float 1D
- Single Float 1D
- Extended Float 1D
- Complex Double Float 1D
- Complex Single Float 1D
- Complex Extended Float 1D
- I8 1D
- I16 1D
- I32 1D
- I64 1D
- U8 1D
- U16 1D
- U32 1D
- U64 1D
Removed the vector and interator  interfaces and its use within the Waveform type since interfaces are not supported in LV2019
</Release_Notes>
    </Description>
